# Layout since the restructure of 2026-10-02: aggregator/{instrument,handler,input,runs/<run>}, coder/, orchestrator/.
# Every run's own Claude login and live session store, wherever a run sits: never committed
**/CONTROL/.cc/
# per run: a stray _to_delete/ (J, 2026-10-06: nothing set aside stays in the repository; it goes to Jail/_to_delete/
# under its path, and the acceptance tests keep their files there too); interviews' own folders (each a restored checkpoint; rendered settings
# hold full paths); checkpoints (a full copy of the analyst's folder per leg: git already holds every leg's
# files through publish.sh's commit at each close, and a tarball over 100 MB stops every push)
aggregator/runs/*/_to_delete/
aggregator/runs/*/interview-workspaces/
# per run: the Claude leg handler's records (legs.py; 2026-10-05): the sessions' streams, requests and replies. Your
# words to legs go to CONTROL/messages-to-legs.jsonl, which is committed. An interview's own folder never is.
aggregator/runs/*/CONTROL/legs/
# interview transcripts (J, 2026-10-06): each is committed only if J decides so, interview by interview, with
# git add -f. interview.sh copies its transcript to interviews/; at E2a step.sh copies every interview listed in
# CONTROL/interviews.tsv into the analyst's handling/interviews/. CONTROL/interviews.tsv, the list, is committed.
aggregator/runs/*/interviews/
aggregator/runs/*/00_GIVE-THE-AGENT/handling/interviews/
aggregator/runs/*/CONTROL/snapshots/
# analysis branches (legs.py branch; 2026-10-05): a branch's run folder, <parent>--<name>, never reaches main;
# branches.py commits it to its own Git branch, analysis/<run>, under its parent's folder
aggregator/runs/*--*/
# the analyst's settings are rendered per machine at each step; they hold this machine's full paths
aggregator/runs/*/00_GIVE-THE-AGENT/.claude/settings.json
# the raw record for E1's quote check (build_raw_record.py): every frame room's coder corpus, kept on disk;
# MANIFEST.tsv and README.md are committed
aggregator/input/raw/*/
# the harness test's stand-in for the claude command, a link with this machine's path
aggregator/handler/claude/tests/bin/
# the handler's scratch (legacy rooms, lineage) and its machine-specific paths (copy paths.example.json)
aggregator/handler/_work/
aggregator/handler/paths.json
# the Codex runtime's state lives beside the repository (.rplace-runtime-v43/), never in it; this keeps out a stray copy
.rplace-runtime/
# the OpenAI controller's launcher holds the live panel token (its serve() writes it at each start): never committed
Manual-html/OPENAI-LIVE.html
_codex_migration/
# the agents' installed tools in the Orchestrator (a Python, its virtual environment, caches): not records
orchestrator/*/*/python/
orchestrator/*/*/venv/
orchestrator/*/*/uv-cache/
orchestrator/*/*/tooling/
orchestrator/*/*/tmp/
_to_delete/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
*.tmp
*.part

# data/: the downloaded and built stores stay out of git; the scripts, READMEs, LINKs and the atlas are in
data/pixels/*.xz
data/pixels/*.png
data/pixels/*.csv
data/pixels/*.part
data/pixels/reddit-place-username-hashes/
data/users/*/
!data/users/
data/users/worklist.csv.gz
data/users/_users.csv
data/venues-placers/*.jsonl
data/venues-placers/*.manifest.json
data/venues-placers/_shards/
data/raw24/*.jsonl
data/raw24/*.manifest.json
data/raw24/_collected/
data/raw24/venues.txt
data/pixels-per-artwork/_work/
data/pixels-per-artwork/inputs/
data/pixels-per-artwork/data/
data/pixels-hourly/_*.jsonl*
data/pixels-hourly/pixels.csv
data/atlas/*.json

!data/atlas/derived_regions.json

# set aside before the first push (2026-10-02): earlier file versions live in archive/instrument-history.tar.gz; test residue
aggregator/instrument/_versions/
aggregator/handler/out/
aggregator/runs/*/CONTROL/.compact-gate.*.acceptance.json
